{Opening was a Ruy Lopez... "Gurnhill as White had to seal his 25th move, and
spent some time examining the position. He worked out his intended
continuation several moves deep, and then inadvertently wrote down the second
move of the line instead of the first. When the envelope was opened at the
second sitting it was found that this move was illegal in the diagrammed
position, and the tournament director was forced, on being consulted, to award
Rhodes the game under the rules. This was indeed a sad blow for Gurnhill,
although he can have the satis­faction of having discovered a new kind of
fatal blunder! It would be interesting to know whether this incident has any
close parallel in first class contests." Source: CHESS, August 1945, Vol.10/
119, p184}  0-1

